# FandomVerse — ReadMe

## Project Overview
A React-based fandom hub aggregating Characters, Articles, and Polls across 7 categories (Anime, Gaming, Movies, TV Shows, K-pop, Comics, Manga). Built with Vite, React Router, and static JSON data.

## Quick Start
```bash
npm install
npm run dev
# Opens http://localhost:5173
```

## Project Structure
```
src/
├── components/       # Reusable UI (Card, FilterBar, etc.)
├── pages/            # Route-level views (Hub, Detail, Bookmarks)
├── hooks/            # useFilters, useBookmarks
├── data/             # JSON datasets (characters, articles, polls)
├── styles/           # Global + component CSS (custom properties)
├── App.jsx           # Home + global nav
├── main.jsx          # Router + entry
└── index.css         # Theme tokens, fonts, base styles
```

## Key Features
- **Category hubs** with tabbed sections (Characters / Articles / Polls)
- **Unified FilterBar** — search, category, sort, time-range, bookmarked-only
- **Bookmarks** persisted in localStorage, accessible via `/bookmarks`
- **Per-category theming** via `--accent` CSS variable
- **Editorial article layout** with sections, pull quotes, responsive typography
- **Poll visualization** with ranked bars and percentages

## Data Model
- **Characters**: 30 entries, linked by `id`, `slug`, `category`, `franchise`
- **Articles**: 7 entries, linked by `slug`, `category`, `publishedDate`
- **Polls**: 14 entries, linked by `id`, `category`, `totalVotes`

## Assumptions
1. No backend/auth — bookmarks use localStorage only
2. Static JSON content — no CMS
3. Images hosted externally (MyAnimeList, TMDB, CDN)
4. Client-side filtering — suitable for <500 items per type
5. Modern browsers only (CSS `color-mix()`, custom properties)
6. English-only, no i18n
7. SPA — React Router, no SSR

## Scripts
| Command | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| `npm run dev` | Start dev server (HMR) |
| `npm run build` | Production build to `/dist` |
| `npm run preview` | Preview production build |

## Deployment
Static output in `/dist` — deploy to Vercel, Netlify, GitHub Pages, or any static host.

## Team Distribution (Original)
